## Not adopted (per Aegis AI security principles)

The following ideas from the surveyed repos were explicitly **not** adopted
because they conflict with Aegis AI's owner-only/consent/grounding principles:

* Runtime self-installing skills from the internet (adirangel/JARVIS) —
  prohibited by the Aegis AI master prompt.
* Unrestricted desktop control / screen-vision identification of people
  (PanPenek/JarvisAi) — would violate the "never identify strangers" principle.
* Auto-purchases or financial transactions — out of scope for a camera assistant.
